{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth","id":838157,"title":"Acadia: Lower Depth?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T12:02:18-08:00","id":838157,"title":"Acadia: Lower Depth?","content":"From what we know of Mage 2e and Changeling 2e, would Arcadia be more likely to be one of the Lower Depths, part of the Fallen World, or a part of the Supernatural Realms?<br /> <br /> I personally lean towards part of the Lower Depths, it shares thematic elements with Supernatural Arcadia, but at the end of the day it functions very different from Supernatural Arcadia. Supernatural Arcadia doesn't suffer from lack of creativity for example.<br /> <br /> The Hedge could be like an Verge or Emanation.<br /> <br /> Plus I like that its kind of a trap for mages, its this weird mystery, it resembles Arcadia even more then Inferno resembles Pandomiem, or Duat resembles Stygia, so it can easily confuse a mage and leave them in danger.<br /> <br /> Like Venus Fly Trap.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the other splats will be mentioned at all in 2e beyond the Toyko Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:07:52-08:00","id":838163,"title":"","content":"This notion has been raised before, and as far as I recall the consensus ranged from &quot;This is an interesting idea&quot; to &quot;Get you're goddamn mage-centric cosmology out of my Changeling&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:15:23-08:00","id":838293,"title":"","content":"I personally lean towards it being a Lower Depth realm inhabited by (created by?) The Old Gods of Thistle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:34:41-08:00","id":838300,"title":"","content":"While I dislike Mage attempts to explain the wider cosmology, my personal way to make Arcadia fit would be as a Lower Depth whose signature lack is Creativity. While the fantastical nature of Arcadia seems whimsical to us, it still abides by very hard and fast rules of Wyrd, Fate, and narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:37:44-08:00","id":838302,"title":"","content":"Count me in the second camp Elfive listed.<br /> <br /> One thing I want to bring up is that Lower Depths are considered part of the Fallen World. If it ain't the Supernal or the Abyss, it's the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Also, David Brookshaw has gone out of his way to make it clear that the Supernal Arcadia and Fae Arcadia are very probably not the same place, with the tiniest of possibility it is. It is a stance David Hill has supported, as have most of the writers. If not all of them.<br /> <br /> THat's all I have to say on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:11:21-08:00","id":838584,"title":"","content":"I have a general distaste towards Mages being right about things, so when a question pops up that can be summed up as &quot;Is X actually [Mage thing]?&quot; my default answer is &quot;no, but Mages think it is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:17:50-08:00","id":838608,"title":"","content":"How about this for something to completely blow your mind. Changeling Arcadia != Realm of the Thistle. Changeling Arcadia = the whole of the Supernal, above and beyond what the mages have Watchtowers in.<br /> <br /> Exarchs kicking out the Old Gods? Ha. They might have successfully claimed a Title or ten, but that's considered amusing by all the other Gentry running around, and consider it a challenge. The Exarchs need followers for their eternal war holding on to their thrones!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:40:35-08:00","id":838683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838608#post838608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this for something to completely blow your mind. Changeling Arcadia != Realm of the Thistle. Changeling Arcadia = the whole of the Supernal, above and beyond what the mages have Watchtowers in.<br /> <br /> Exarchs kicking out the Old Gods? Ha. They might have successfully claimed a Title or ten, but that's considered amusing by all the other Gentry running around, and consider it a challenge. The Exarchs need followers for their eternal war holding on to their thrones!</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, if we take at least some of the Fae as being kicked out Supernal creatures, you might be onto something. What mages percieve as two Arcadias technically *are*, but only in this timeline. Parts taken by Exarchs versus this timelines' kicked out Gods. The Hedge (and probably Supernal Arcadia too) is essentially a gateway to different realities and timelines.<br /> <br /> Dave said that the Arcadias aren't the same, but also explained that the relationship is somewhat... complicated:<br /> <i>Originally posted by <b>Dave Brookshaw</b></i><br /> <i>Okay, so. Bear with me here.<br /> <br /> I'm going to explain how emanations and supernal symbols work. I'm going to use Arcadia as an entirely hypothetical example. The example is not canon. But you'll get why.<br /> <br /> So.<br /> <br /> Here's how reality forms.<br /> <br /> first we have raw, undifferentiated potential. This might be the supernal without a filter, or it might bete theoretical Empyrean.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Supernal, which is made up of every possible Truth, expressed as symbols.<br /> <br /> Then we have Emanations, which are more solid, and based around particular symbols.<br /> <br /> (Then the Abyss cracks reality in half, introducing Lies to mis it up a little)<br /> <br /> Then the Phenomenal world.<br /> <br /> <br /> When Archmages enter the Supernal, they become symbols. When they interact with the other symbols, they can change them, often without meaning to. Everything below the Supernal is defined by it.<br /> <br /> Gods are just symbols of self-aware things; they think because they should think.<br /> <br /> So, in our example. We have a group of Supernal symbols that we'll call &quot;The Old Gods of Thistle&quot;. Because they exist, an Emanation Realm we'll call &quot;Faerie&quot; also exists &quot;below&quot; them. Whenever they're redefined, Faerie will change to suit.<br /> <br /> So our Exarch-symbols stomp in and kill them all. Faerie ceases to exist. But wait! We clap our hands, and remember that these Old Gods of Thistle symbols have an optional at best relationship to time. So the Exarchs have/will/will have been/whenfore kill/ing/ed them. So what? They keep coming back, and they've never been away. <br /> <br /> And Faerie keeps coming back, and has never been away.<br /> <br /> Our bullying Exarch-symbols exclaim &quot;fuck it&quot;, and head back/will head back/have headed back to the symbols of things they understand, like &quot;important people drive history&quot; and &quot;everything falls apart&quot;. You know. Symbols humans can understand. The four-fifths of the Supernal that has the good grace to be conquered after they've conquered it, rather than before or sideways, is good enough. There are even an infinite number of time-symbols that place themselves after the event. Good solid Time- and Fate- symbols that a person can get their head around. Not these stories.<br /> <br /> When someone becomes an archmage, they gather up the symbols of the things that were attracted to their Mystery Play and turn them into a Cintamani, which is Archmage-speak for &quot;the symbol of 'I'm an archmage'&quot;. This means that everything made by those symbols gets altered, which makes new archmages cry until they become numbed to the transhuman gnostic horror of their existence (tm). But it's okay, because they're now an archmage. They're a archmage because the Supernal says they're an archmage.<br /> <br /> The Golden Road Ascension is when an Archmage then goes &quot;so... If I were to Be an Archmage back down below, and, say, convince the two Wings that they're same order and that magic is alive, then return to the supernal, I'll have attracted the symbols of the two orders and magic's not-aliveness toward the symbol of &quot;I'm totally an archmaster&quot;. I can then use the same trick as in my Threshold to hammer them into shape. Back down below will conform, I'll always have been right and if I do it enough times, maybe I can make a symbol of &quot;The Mysterium ( ps I'm Ascended)&quot; out of them all.<br /> <br /> But I digress.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Exarchs attack the Old Gods (and again, because of Time they're always and never attacking them now, tommorow and yesterday). The Old Gods get changed in the struggle, and Faerie gets changed as the Supernal symbols of Faerie alter. To make matters worse, when they sometimes/always/sometime/never win, te Exarchs kick Gods out down into the horrid realms of solidity and such. Sometimes, the Old Gods land in Faerie and go native, accepting a bit more reality. And because Time, they're constantly doing so.<br /> <br /> Is Changeling Arcadia...<br /> <br /> 1) The &quot;Faerie&quot; Emanation, occupied by continously exiled story-beings, with the &quot;Wyld&quot; being the Supernal?<br /> 2) The conglomerate of &quot;Faerie&quot; symbols in the Supernal, with the Wyld being the Empyrean?<br /> 3) A combination of the two - it IS possible to get from an Emanation to the supernal, after all. Arcadia is the border between them, the Emanation meeting the symbol-beings?<br /> 4) Lots of Emanations, one for each story-creature, with easy routes between them?<br /> <br /> Because Time, it's all four at once. And never. Whenever you walk the Hedge, be careful, for you don't know which Hedge you're walking. And none of them lead anywhere good for a human, with their quaint notions of cause and effect, should go. And because the story-beings find notions like &quot;we should stick with one version of ourselves&quot; incomprehensible, they're interacting with one another! Option 1 above lives quite happily overlaid over Options 2to 3, and multiple versions of the same story-being exist in the same metaphysical space. <br /> <br /> And this is why Arcadia is unknowable. It's a great big smudge on your map, thanks to Time not really existing in that &quot;part&quot; of the Supernal. The titanomachy, the Ascension War and the end of the world are all happening &quot;at once&quot;. Everything that's ever happened, or ever will, to Arcadia already exists and has ended in Arcadia. The Old Gods of Thistle are incapable of interacting with linear time properly, because they ARE narrative time. If they could be MADE to, if someone managed to Ascend redefining the entire mess as being in the &quot;past&quot; and have that mean something, then they'd instantly have been killed. Good luck Sealing an Omen that says all stories have already ended, though. <br /> <br /> What a Changeling experiences is well-described. What that means, though, from an Archmaster's point of view is &quot;system error. Does not parse&quot;.<br /> <br /> There is no answer to the Arcadia question. <br /> The answer to the Arcadia question is &quot;yes/no/fnord/it was a dark and stormy night&quot;.<br /> <br /> Bloody Faeries.</i><br /> <br /> Bloody Faeries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:51:08-08:00","id":838690,"title":"","content":"I never liked that explanation, no offence to Dave Brookshaw's impeccable writing. I just have a general distaste for one thing that should be equal to the others being somehow &quot;more special&quot; than the others. Kind of why I struggle with Mage a lot, despite how much some of it appeals to me.<br /> <br /> I tend to resolve The Arcadia Problem by not using the canon Paths and simply making up my own. There is only one Arcadia, and that's Changeling Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:56:45-08:00","id":838695,"title":"","content":"Luckily, you are both right, although sadly neither of you are... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:04:47-08:00","id":838700,"title":"","content":"On the Mage map of reality, Arcadia is a roaming circus. Is it in the Lower Depths? Sometimes. Is it part of Supernal Arcadia? Only on the third Tuesday of the month. In the Abyss? Now and then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:45:03-08:00","id":838715,"title":"","content":"The really cool thing about the Realm of Narrative Causality is that it being whatever you need or want it to be for the game you're running is <i>metaphysically consistent</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:59:07-08:00","id":838719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838683#post838683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bloody Faeries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as the guy who earned 10 likes by posting the exact same thing in a Mage thread, I would like to point out that, since then, Dave has stated <i>several times</i> since then that he doesn't consider that to actually be a true summation, as far as canon works. Although the way Arcadia works certainly is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:09:50-08:00","id":838721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838683#post838683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if we take at least some of the Fae as being kicked out Supernal creatures, you might be onto something.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I'm not. I have a heavily houseruled crossover setting where I'm debating on making it true (because eff the sandbox worlds), because I like the idea of a give-take rivalry relationship between mages and fae in general. Much like you have vampires and werewolves with their odd relationship as rival predators. <br /> <br /> If you don't mind the houserules, it could be a pretty kick ass setting feature for crossover.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:42:07-08:00","id":838731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838719#post838719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as the guy who earned 10 likes by posting the exact same thing in a Mage thread, I would like to point out that, since then, Dave has stated <i>several times</i> since then that he doesn't consider that to actually be a true summation, as far as canon works. Although the way Arcadia works certainly is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he's been quite clear that while the answer to the Arcadia question may have been &quot;yes/no/fnord/it was a dark and stormy night&quot; in 1e, in 2e it's &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the question of Arcadia being a Lower Depth? I honestly think the question is a bit tautological. A &quot;Lower Depth&quot; isn't really a thing that exists, it's more of a classification Mages give to places. If Mages call someplace a Lower Depth, they do so because it matches the criteria they've decided make someplace a Lower Depth. It's like if you decided to call things that are yellow &quot;Hasturians.&quot; Is a lemon a Hasturian? Sure, since that's what you've decided &quot;Hasturian&quot; means. But, like, so what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:55:57-08:00","id":838735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838731#post838731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, he's been quite clear that while the answer to the Arcadia question may have been &quot;yes/no/fnord/it was a dark and stormy night&quot; in 1e, in 2e it's &quot;no&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then Arcadia realises it was running off the wrong edition two seconds after the bridge to the supernal closes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T12:25:42-08:00","id":838748,"title":"","content":"So Changeling Arcadia is the Supernatural Arcadia, is an emanation realm, is a place which is part of the above part of Fallen Realm along side earth, the shadow,and the underworld, and apart of the lower depths, and none of the above, at the same time.<br /> <br /> Interesting philosphically, but in practice hard to do anything practical with that.<br /> <br /> Honestly for my mind, I'll just keep it as a Lower Depths plane, that mimics a Supernatural Realm enough to cause confusion and danger to mages, and which may have a histotical conection to the Supernatural Arcadia adding to the mages confusion.<br /> <br /> Its simply easier for practical use then the other choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T12:37:42-08:00","id":838750,"title":"","content":"Seconding Charlaquin's note that treating Mage cosmology as &quot;correct&quot; is engaging in the Sharpshooter Fallacy writ large.<br /> <br /> Call it tautological, but as far as I consider the question to particularly matter, Faerie is the place/&quot;place&quot; nearest to the Wyrd in the same sense that facilities are part of the God-Machine and the qashmallim are made of the Divine Fire. It's not like with the Arisen and Sekhem, where their entire model is built on taking a particular type of magic out of the world and putting it into another dimension \u2014 goblin markets notwithstanding, fae cosmology is much more concerned with tit-for-tat and meddling in worldly affairs than harvesting agency and sentiment from the universe.<br /> <br /> Treating Faerie as a Lower Depth would mean assuming it's one that's somehow closer to Earth than the Inferno, which is about as close as the Depths normally get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-28-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T12:42:45-08:00","id":838754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838163#post838163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This notion has been raised before, and as far as I recall the consensus ranged from &quot;This is an interesting idea&quot; to &quot;Get you're goddamn mage-centric cosmology out of my Changeling&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my POV, it's very much more &quot;get your changeling cosmology out of my Mage.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T12:53:21-08:00","id":838762,"title":"","content":"Actually, I've thought of a better analogy. Pluto. Pluto is a roughly spherical celestial object that orbits the sun. Prior to 2006, astronomers called roughly spherical celestial objects that orbit stars &quot;planets&quot;. Then, in 2006, a committee of the world's leading astronomers got together and decided that the definition of &quot;Planet&quot; was too broad, and from then on they were only going to call roughly spherical celestial objects that orbit stars <i>and don't have any other similar-sized celestial objects within a certain radius of their orbital path</i> planets. If you were not an astronomer or a follower of astronomical news at the time, you were likely confused why the astronomers were suddenly saying Pluto wasn't a planet any more. After all, nothing changed about Pluto. It's still a roughly spherical celestial object that orbits the sun. It still fits the pre-2006 definition of a planet. And if you're not an astronomer or astronomy enthusiast, you might not even be aware that when astronomers say &quot;planet&quot; now they mean something different when what they meant when they said &quot;planet&quot; then. It also probably makes no practical difference in your life if you're not an astronomer.<br /> <br /> Similarly, when Mages say &quot;Lower Depth&quot; they mean a place that lacks a supernal truth and consumes the truth it lacks from the fallen world. Does Arcadia match that definition? I honestly don't know, I was never that into Mage in 1e and my Mage knowledge is pretty much limited to the 2e spoilers and some things I've heard from discussions on these forums. But it also probably makes no practical difference in your character's lives unless your characters are Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-28-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:21:25-08:00","id":838774,"title":"","content":"My understanding of the Lower Depths seems to tell me that mage's best <i>hypothesis</i> is that it's places lacking in one or more of the Arcana, or some element of reality.<br /> <br /> I don't know if anyone has ever verified that as an absolute truth(Truth) yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:32:49-08:00","id":838776,"title":"","content":"I think Truth in Changeling is a negotiable concept, just like everything else.<br /> <br /> Something can be True if you give Truth something it wants in return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:37:40-08:00","id":838779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838774#post838774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of the Lower Depths seems to tell me that mage's best <i>hypothesis</i> is that it's places lacking in one or more of the Arcana, or some element of reality.<br /> <br /> I don't know if anyone has ever verified that as an absolute truth(Truth) yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding - and as I mentioned, it's a limited understanding, so you may know better than me - is that the label &quot;lower depth&quot; doesn't have any actual meaning beyond what Mages give it. Maybe it's like dark matter, in that they observe the effects of Lower Depths and have multiple hypothesies about what they may be, none of which have enough supporting evidence to be considered Theories, let alone Laws. But either way, as a Mage-created name to describe phenomena as Mages observe them, &quot;Lower Depths&quot; pretty much means what ever Mages say it means in the context of Mage, and pretty much has no meaning outside of that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:42:29-08:00","id":838780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838776#post838776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Truth in Changeling is a negotiable concept, just like everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Truths that Mage deals with aren't something you can actually identify except through metaphor. The mystery that tells fire what it is is a Truth, not a truth. You don't really negotiate that in any sense but the navigational.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:44:51-08:00","id":838782,"title":"","content":"You can literally buy and sell metaphors at a goblin market though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:45:36-08:00","id":838783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838782#post838782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can literally buy and sell metaphors at a goblin market though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can buy and sell masks, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:53:51-08:00","id":838786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838780#post838780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Truths that Mage deals with aren't something you can actually identify except through metaphor. The mystery that tells fire what it is is a Truth, not a truth. You don't really negotiate that in any sense but the navigational.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the Contracts deal with abstract concepts and things without a physical representation (such as Time, Space, Metaphysical Change, Emotion and Authority). If changelings can make bargains with such things, I can't see why they can't make a bargain with Truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:54:37-08:00","id":838787,"title":"","content":"You can assume that if I mention a capital T Truth in casual context, I'm talking from a mage perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:02:44-08:00","id":838793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838754#post838754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my POV, it's very much more &amp;quot;get your changeling cosmology out of my Mage.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> am I the only one who prefers a cohesive Chonicle of Darkness cosmology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:04:33-08:00","id":838796,"title":"","content":"Nope.<br /> <br /> I'm not one of those who prefers it, but even among writers, people do like it.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean we'll deliver it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:08:59-08:00","id":838798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838793#post838793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am I the only one who prefers a cohesive Chonicle of Darkness cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say you're part of a vast majority. People like it when everything fits neatly in its proper place.<br /> <br /> Normally, I'd be right with you, but not with Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:14:59-08:00","id":838799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838748#post838748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly for my mind, I'll just keep it as a Lower Depths plane, that mimics a Supernatural Realm enough to cause confusion and danger to mages, and which may have a histotical conection to the Supernatural Arcadia adding to the mages confusion.<br /> <br /> Its simply easier for practical use then the other choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is my understanding from Dave's other comments that Mages are not in any way confused about the differences in the Arcadias, particularly in 2e where the Supernal World is far more pronounced, pervasive and casually observed with Mage Sight, unlike the far off Supernal Realms of Mage 1e. <br /> <br /> When an Acanthus summons a being from Supernal Arcadia, no one who has any understanding of Changeling and Mage cosmologies (both IC and OOC) would mistake them for Gentry. <br /> <br /> Individual mages may be curious about changelings, the Wyrd, the Hedge, Gentry, goblins, and even Changeling Arcadia itself, etc., as is the nature of mages to be inquisitive, if not obsessive, about all supernatural phenomena, beings and places, but they would not mistake any of those things with Supernal Arcadia any more than they would be confused about angels and demoms of the God Machine and the beings of the Aether and Pandemonium, ghosts with shades from Stygia, or spirits with the beasts and totems of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:19:25-08:00","id":838801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838793#post838793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> am I the only one who prefers a cohesive Chonicle of Darkness cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because not everything fits into Mages' cosmological theories doesn't mean the cosmology isn't cohesive. It just means it's bigger than Mages know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:19:27-08:00","id":838802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838793#post838793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> am I the only one who prefers a cohesive Chonicle of Darkness cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The lack of cohesiveness in the overall cosmology, the gaps, questions and outright inconsistencies, help reinforce the mystery and horror of the overall CofD setting. <br /> <br /> It is a feature, not a bug. It also far more easily permits new additions to the setting as new games are developed and published. A static or rigid cosmology potentially inhibits long-term developmental creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:52:24-08:00","id":838820,"title":"","content":"My personal interpretation is that the Fall left what used to be a precise, well-ordered cosmology in a jumbled heap on the metaphorical floor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:53:01-08:00","id":838821,"title":"","content":"If there is a cohesion point in the CHronicles, it is, by the inherent laws in it's nature, unknowable. Or, at the least, the greatest mystery of all.<br /> <br /> Plus, honestly, it's more fun for players to come up with their own answers than it is to supply one.<br /> <br /> And for me, it's more fun to just say &quot;Fuck the answer, I'm never going to do anything with it. Confusion is the reward.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:18:37-08:00","id":838826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838786#post838786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the Contracts deal with abstract concepts and things without a physical representation (such as Time, Space, Metaphysical Change, Emotion and Authority). If changelings can make bargains with such things, I can't see why they can't make a bargain with Truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about truth as an abstract concept. I'm talking about Truths, as in things with no <i>direct conceptual</i> representation in worldly experience. The only unifying factor they have is that they all inform some aspect of reality and can be partially understood through those aspects.<br /> <br /> Making a Contract with Truth in that sense would be like making a contract with God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:30:21-08:00","id":838831,"title":"","content":"You mean Mage like Platonic Truths, THE TRUTH,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T16:10:30-08:00","id":838840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838826#post838826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about truth as an abstract concept. I'm talking about Truths, as in things with no <i>direct conceptual</i> representation in worldly experience. The only unifying factor they have is that they all inform some aspect of reality and can be partially understood through those aspects.<br /> <br /> Making a Contract with Truth in that sense would be like making a contract with God.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having an FMA flashback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T17:05:09-08:00","id":838870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838840#post838840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having an FMA flashback.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://shinmaru.files.wordpress.com/2010/06/truthgetsit.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:46:02-08:00","id":838930,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think a cohesive cosmology could do anything but hurt CoD. Contrary to some people who have posted here, I think that Mages being broadly and catastrophically wrong about the nature of reality pretty much demolishes the themes of their gameline. At the same time, their being right about everything they believe would do the same to a lot of other gamelines. The best solution, in my mind, is that <i>every</i> splat is right; it's actually the everyday mortals who are wrong.<br /> <br /> Mortals being wrong is nothing new in the CoD, of course. Most of them don't believe in the supernatural <i>at all</i>, or else only believe in a fairly specific collection of supernatural things that are part of their religious and cultural upbringing. But if mortals are wrong about Vampires and Werewolves and Fairies and a hundred other things, why should we be surprised that some of their basic assumptions about the universe are wrong as well?<br /> <br /> Mortals, on the whole, expect the universe to make sense. They believe that there are objective truths about the universe that can be observed, quantified, and understood by the human mind, even if we haven't uncovered them all yet. To me, that seems like exactly the kind of expectation that the world of the CoD likes to defy. I think that perhaps the most basic, overarching theme of the CoD is that <i>the world is stranger than we know</i>, and that doesn't just mean that there are monsters hiding in every dark corner. It means that basic deductive logic sometimes breaks down, that mutually exclusive things can be simultaneously true, and that the universe laughs in the face of your attempts to chart its structure. And honestly, that's something I really like about the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T20:44:10-08:00","id":838941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838750#post838750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding Charlaquin's note that treating Mage cosmology as &amp;quot;correct&amp;quot; is engaging in the Sharpshooter Fallacy writ large.<br /> <br /> Call it tautological, but as far as I consider the question to particularly matter, Faerie is the place/&amp;quot;place&amp;quot; nearest to the Wyrd in the same sense that facilities are part of the God-Machine and the qashmallim are made of the Divine Fire. It's not like with the Arisen and Sekhem, where their entire model is built on taking a particular type of magic out of the world and putting it into another dimension \u2014 goblin markets notwithstanding, fae cosmology is much more concerned with tit-for-tat and meddling in worldly affairs than harvesting agency and sentiment from the universe.<br /> <br /> Treating Faerie as a Lower Depth would mean assuming it's one that's somehow closer to Earth than the Inferno, which is about as close as the Depths normally get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it seems clear to me that what the True Fae &quot;devour&quot; from the world to Arcadia is creativity, some things are tit for tat, but creativity and imagination that Arcadia depends on comes from our world, Arcadia is dependant on it for its form and function. Yes Arcadia seems like its this place of wonder and magic, and it is, but its wonder and magic that is born from Ironside and to a lesser extent the Underworld and the Shadow. It seems more wonderous there because that borrowed magic and imagination aren't counter acted by the forces of stablity and normal reality that the &quot;normal world&quot; is, so while objective reality stops fantasy from = reality, in Arcadia they only steal the fantasy/emotion part, which means it defines Arcadia's reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T20:51:19-08:00","id":838943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838941#post838941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it seems clear to me that what the True Fae &quot;devour&quot; from the world to Arcadia is creativity, some things are tit for tat, but creativity and imagination that Arcadia depends on comes from our world, Arcadia is dependant on it for its form and function. Yes Arcadia seems like its this place of wonder and magic, and it is, but its wonder and magic that is born from Ironside and to a lesser extent the Underworld and the Shadow. It seems more wonderous there because that borrowed magic and imagination aren't counter acted by the forces of stablity and normal reality that the &quot;normal world&quot; is, so while objective reality stops fantasy from = reality, in Arcadia they only steal the fantasy/emotion part, which means it defines Arcadia's reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of what you're describing applies any less to the Shadow and the Underworld. There is very little of the raw supernatural that <i>does</i> have creativity and imagination of its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:36:10-08:00","id":840419,"title":"","content":"All Tigers have stripes. But are all striped things Tigers?<br /> <br /> All Lower Depths lack essential reality. But are all places that lack essential reality Lower Depths?<br /> <br /> Another thing; what determines which parts of Reality are essential?<br /> <br /> If Arcadia being a Lower Depth fits your Chronicle plans. Go for it. It wouldn't be the first time a whole 'Supernatural Space' landed there. Just look at Hell. Assuming Arcadia is a Lower Depth. It is soundly a part of the Fallen's gutted corpse and the Hedge is either a Chamber-Realm or another Lower Depth entirely that just happens to act as a transition. Lower Depth Arcadia is NOT Supernal.<br /> <br /> In my understanding. The Lower Depths are a mix of Exarch experimentation in exerting control over the Fallen, and bits of the Fallen that broke off during the Fall of the Celestial Ladder.<br /> Fae Arcadia is like a dark wood bordering the Phenominal/Material/Sane clearing Mortals dwell within. It's a place <i>beside</i>, <i>other</i>, and <i>beyond</i>. What that means for Mage is irrelevant outside the context of Mage. Arcadia is Fairy. And Fairy is power. Whether Fae and the Exarchs match up in power is a Mage question. Why should Changelings give a fuck about disembodied Master-Archwizards out in Magic-space? They have the Lady of the Dew hunting them down and need a place to hide tonight!<br /> <br /> I wish The Shadow and the Underworld got these kinds of treatment. Arcadia and the Astral are spoiled on all this hypothetical navel-gazing. I want to know more about the Border Marches of old and the boundary space beyond Gaia's embrace.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:00:08-08:00","id":840429,"title":"","content":"I'd lean toward it being in the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; in the sense that &quot;Lower Depths&quot; are a catchall to refer to where Mage understood cosmology stuffs the things that can't be classified in the relationship between between the Phenomenal/Fallen and the Supernal, rather than a metaphysically coherent category in its own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:02:26-08:00","id":840430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838157-acadia-lower-depth?p=838793#post838793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> am I the only one who prefers a cohesive Chonicle of Darkness cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If we had that, there'd be a lot less Mysteries for Mages to investigate. The cosmos is much bigger and more complicated than can be easily categorized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]